 this is also my go-to with a couple of  slight adjustments depending on the team  i'm running with for the first raid  which we all know is all about dps  it's pretty much an all-round build it's  adequate but  not particularly amazing or specialized  in any particular area  originally built for the lmg rifle combo  because my favorite archetype assault  rifles  were pretty lackluster on release but  these days it runs pretty good for both  first we have the coyotes exotic mask  for a big boost to critical hit chance  and damage  the backpack the providence defense with  vigilance  with attributes rolled into critical hit  chance and critical hit damage  in the vest slot is providence defense  with unbreakable  with attributes rolled into critical hit  chance and critical hit damage  unbreakable for the solo player helps  with survivability  in a team situation you may want to try  glass cannon for extra damage  for the gloves i'm using contractor's  petrol's defense with the spare  attribute  rolled into critical hit damage  in this slot is the cesca holster with  attributes rolled into critical hit  charts  and critical hit damage  the knee pads are fox's prayer overlord  armaments with the spare attribute  rolled into critical hit damage  [Music]  the skills are the reviver hive because  you know  solo player and the fixer drone just to  take the edge off some of the incoming  damage  this is kind of a free slot that'll  often change out depending on what i'm  coming up against  the primary weapons include the famas  with the killer talent  which is great for [ __ ] builds and the  classic m1a with rifleman  to give a bit of range plus it hits like  a truck  for the sidearm any pistol with the  finisher talent will do the job  all that critical hit damage adds up  for the specialization i'm using gunner  for the amaron kill  plus the ammo over time comes in quite  useful for some of the directives  the name pays homage to my diablo 2  roots  basically this build is good for running  through content fast  built purely around dps and life  leeching talents what  well armor leeching talents the idea is  to never stop shooting  or you'll die the gameplay style  requires you to be up front  in the thick of the action although it  can be run in heroic difficulty  it's certainly much better suited to  challenging or below  this is the sort of build that i would  use from push for time and need to run  through bounties or missions as quickly  as possible  first we have the hunter's fury mask  with all attributes rolled into critical  hit chance and critical hit damage  for the backpack we're using the memento  exotic you are up front and center  hard against the enemies so collecting  these trophies are easy to achieve  this will give increased weapon damage  armor and skill efficiency  in the vest slot the bellstone armory  with intimidate  with all attributes rolled to critical  hit chance and critical hit damage  the intimidate talent synchronizes well  with the momento backpack  providing a 35 boost to weapon damage  for the gloves hunter's fury with the  spare attribute rolled into critical hit  damage  the holster is also hunter's fury again  with attributes rolled into critical hit  damage  yet again the knee pads are hunter's  fury with the attribute rolled into  critical hit damage  the skills being used are the reviver  hive and the crusader ballistic shield  i'm generally not a fan of running  shields but given how close you need to  get to the npcs this can really help  soak up some of that damage before you  get to the point of taking down the  targets  the primary weapons include the  chatterbox exotic smg  which is great for this build you need  to be up close anyway where smgs are in  their element  plus it gets a buff from the hunter's  fury set and this talent can be used to  keep your magazine full of ammo as well  as increase your rate of fire  the other weapon is up to you if you're  using the chatterbox you probably won't  be changing over too often  here i'm using the mop shotgun for more  armor on kill  again the sidearm is up to you i use the  kdi card custom  which gives another skill tier towards  my shield  for the specialization i'm using gunner  for even more armor on kill  and the fact that the ammo slowly  replenishes helps keep you moving  forward  and reducing the need to collect ammo  in my opinion still the strongest type  of build you can make in the division 2  especially with the more recent update  adding gear that can get even  greater numbers out of your skills it  certainly isn't the most exciting way of  playing the game  having your skills do most of the damage  but don't think that this means you just  deploy  and sit back to get the most out of this  build you still need to be shooting  and a lot as i may have already implied  this build is suited to all situations  but can be a little slow so the best  place to use this  is with the most difficult content  personally i really only use this build  for legendary missions these days  which will give you the greatest chance  for completion with the least amount of  player skill required  for the mask i'm using the impress  international with attributes rolled  into skill damage  and haste the backpack is hanayu  with perfect combined arms attributes  are rolled into skill damage  and haste combined arms increases your  skill damage  after hitting an enemy with your weapon  in the vest slot we have the wyven wear  with kinetic momentum  with attributes rolled into skill damage  and haste you should be seeing a trend  here  the gloves are empress international  with attributes rolled into skill damage  and haste again  the holster is the waveform exotic this  will provide another massive buff to  your skill damage  and the knee pads are hanayu yet again  with attributes rolled into skill damage  and haste the skills being used are the  striker drone and assault turret  arguably the drone is more important  even though it does less damage  and has a tendency to get stuck in  random places all the time  the fact that it isn't stationary it  will go off and chase npcs out of hiding  which reduces the need for you to go out  into the open and given that you're  quite squishy this is definitely a bonus  the primary weapons include the  capacitor exotic assault rifle  for huge buffs to your skill damage and  it also has some fairly decent weapon  damage  and the harmony rifle for a bit of range  plus the perfectly in sync talent  provides a good boost to your skill  damage as well  for the sidearm the maxim 9 pistol is  pretty good  if for some reason you need to pull out  your sidearm this will give you the best  bang for your buck with your skills  due to the perfect spike talent  i've used the technician specialization  the extra skill tear this provides  isn't necessary but it does add another  7.5  weapon damage to the capacitor i prefer  to use it for the extra skill damage  and the bonus damage to drones and  robotics  i must admit after so long it was quite  fun putting this video together  this probably won't be useful to the  majority of you but for those of you who  keep asking what i'm running i now have  something to point you towards  as i said earlier i have a number of  other builds to run too these would just  be the main ones that i play around with  i'm currently working on a sniper build  that works more like the marksman rifle  builds we had in the division one  basically i still want to be able to  one-shot enemies but without the painful  scoping time that has been forced on us  in the division two  anyway thank you very much for watching  though it's been a while since i made  any guides or how-to videos i'm thinking  i might try and pop the odd one out  every now and then  game lore is still my thing and will  still be a priority but for during times  where there is less for me to talk about  it could be something a little different  for me to have a play around with  thanks again cheers  [Music]  okay

